4. She describes British bread as bland and floppy, lacking the texture and taste of European varieties. (Verbatim: "you grab a slice of bread I had this morning, it just kind of flops... it's very uh... soggy without being wet.")

5. She prefers factory-made, pre-sliced bread for convenience due to laziness. (Verbatim: "I go to, we get, usually our bread will be the factory made stuff... I'm lazy.")

