8. She grew up in a household where plates were warmed in the microwave before serving food, especially in cold weather. (Verbatim: "back at my parents... we used to have to put the plates in the microwave and heat the plates up first so the food wouldn't get too cold.")

9. She associates cold climates with the practice of heating plates before meals, suggesting she lived somewhere cold during her upbringing. (Verbatim: "maybe this applies to anyone living somewhere cold... I completely forgot that like I had to do this.")

10. She has a vocabulary influenced by scientific journals, though she typically suppresses it during streams. (Verbatim: "my vocabulary is words used in scientific journals... I lock that away most of the time.") [end of text]



